  Author draft by parent session hairer-codex-existence-20261111, issue #26.
  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. This
  records inspected final calls and candidate canonical suppliers. It is
  <strong|not> an exhaustive proof-coverage or meaning audit, and does not
  discharge an analytic premise merely because a corresponding Lean theorem
  exists. Use the latest entries in <verbatim|reviews/closure-audit.md> for
  current local findings; older chronological entries can be superseded.

  <section|Target and choice order><label|target-and-choice-order>

  Read <verbatim|Lean/ChallengeSpec.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/Solution.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/Construction.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/HierarchyBridge.lean> and
  <verbatim|Lean/TraceBridge.lean> in full.
  <verbatim|YangMills.JointExistence> fixes one Wilson family after a simple
  gauge group has been given. Its regularity precedes the arbitrary strictly
  increasing volume sequence p. Only afterwards are the subsequence q and one
  hierarchy chosen. <verbatim|YangMills.jointExistence> in
  <strong|Solution.lean> obtains <verbatim|YangMills.constructed> at penalty1
  and applies its order clause to (full,p). The Challenge.lean placeholder is
  a different comparator environment; it is not the proof imported by
  Solution.lean. Preserve the existing source-audit record rather than
  interpreting that placeholder as a newly found endpoint axiom.

  The required public conclusions are Wilson convergence, Reconstructed, the
  separated OperatorProductExpansion, and TraceTest. The construction returns
  additional nested/contact/position-test conclusions, which Solution
  forgets. Do not turn every forgotten conclusion into a new exposition
  requirement. Likewise the narrow trace exclusion must not be called a mass
  gap or exclusion of every generalized free field. The independent meaning
  audit remains required.

  <section|Literal internal assembly><label|literal-internal-assembly>

  Read <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Nonperturbative/Continuum.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Nonperturbative/Headlines.lean>, and
  <verbatim|YM/Independent/Core.lean>. Names below are fully qualified at
  first use.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact
  inspected source use>>|<cell|<strong|Required manuscript binding and
  current status>>>|<row|<cell|Native family>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>,
  then <verbatim|YM.Independent.fundedRun>>|<cell|<verbatim|public-run-binding.tex>
  and its evidence retain native postnumeric data on one R,T,W. Already a
  bounded composition proof; every quantitative supplier still needs closure
  in the full audit. No alternate Roll/Novena history.>>|<row|<cell|Funded
  outputs>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.Funded.jewel>,
  <verbatim|.gallery>, <verbatim|.coverage>, <verbatim|.logPackage>,
  Accepted.lean>|<cell|Same attentive application uses literal R.T,
  tuning.receipts, t, accepts, stories, doors, makes, carries, books.
  <verbatim|original-history-portfolio-attachment.tex> is the identity join.
  LogPackage also retains W, poly, halo, sky, silk, tic, fixed100 and
  logCopy. Existing common-funded/observable/OPE chapters supply the asserted
  estimates.>>|<row|<cell|First extraction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded>
  calls <verbatim|YM.PertExtension.Running.extraction> on
  H.jewel.actual>|<cell|First obtain g and all fixed-level coupling limits B.
  This is a countable extraction, before the field refinement. Reuse
  <verbatim|common-scale-selection.tex> and the coupling-limit arguments;
  final audit must check the exact source profile and volume
  uniformity.>>|<row|<cell|Field/stress extraction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>
  in Joint.lean>|<cell|Same bought reception gives Created, Scrim/Velour/Tabs
  and Makes. <verbatim|Ribbons.laurelE/fugacious> form Aroma; actual
  shell-node producer remains in progress. <verbatim|Acme.readyA> uses the
  same stations and free stress to produce physical stress and annular
  charges. <verbatim|actual-stress-normalization.tex> supplies the common
  comparison curve; <verbatim|actual-stress-annulus.tex> is conditional on
  actual shell nodes.>>|<row|<cell|Free inputs>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.maxwell_supplies>,
  then <verbatim|YM.UVNext.FreeStress.fire> in that same call>|<cell|Keep its
  exact derivative scheme, rotation gear, torch, common nonzero coefficient
  and comparison labels. Free flux and finite stress algebra have canonical
  chapters. Fixed-grade silent polar-vector detection/classification remains
  in progress; internal Ward erasure now has the canonical
  free-internal-ward-erasure chapter and a bounded independent pass;
  all-grade polynomial field detection is not a
  substitute.>>|<row|<cell|Physical action>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.station>
  is applied to <verbatim|YM.Outer.miles> and <verbatim|YM.Work.A01.answer>
  through A11 and A13 through A17>|<cell|Packet prices and conservation cone
  have bounded passes. Ward propagation now has a bounded independent pass at
  c8abceb2, including original-table cancellation and finite internal row
  tests. <verbatim|physical-ward-analytic-continuation.tex> and
  <verbatim|physical-angular-actions.tex> are existing canonical proofs at
  their stated inputs; reconstruction and label descent cover later
  consumers. Final audit must check that every listed answer's hypotheses are
  actually instantiated, not simply cite station.>>|<row|<cell|Final
  table>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Org.Commission.picks> and
  <verbatim|YM.Pert.withFinal>, then private Joint.attached>|<cell|Keep one
  S,F,X, c,U,J and the same equations for free W,K,J. Attached uses the fixed
  free stress normalization to supply FirstExtension. Do not select a new
  stress sign or reference representation
  here.>>|<row|<cell|Retention>|<cell|<verbatim|fromFunded> returns g.refine
  w and uses <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Order.retained>>|<cell|All B limits
  survive w. Full mesh is separately supplied by H.jewel.fullMesh through
  <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.Final.from_spec>; no subsequence-to-full-sequence
  inference. Canonical fullmesh chapters and <verbatim|assembly.tex>
  uniqueness lemma address this distinction.>>|<row|<cell|Phases/OPE>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.EveryPhase.all_characters>,
  one <verbatim|YM.OPE.Prescription.chosen>, then one Reader r>|<cell|Same
  F.phase.transport injection, rights and spots enter r. Produce Foundation
  and nesting with the same services. The all-coherent-prescriptions clause
  is separate; do not identify those prescriptions with r. Existing phase,
  OPE-prescription/grid/grouping/estimate chapters are candidate suppliers,
  subject to dependency closure.>>|<row|<cell|Trace>|<cell|<verbatim|Trace.Target.assembled
  F h (Trace.arenaT F h (Trace.crest_ready F h (H.gallery
  f)))>>|<cell|H.gallery applies to every qualifying f,S,F, so it applies to
  this F after refinement. Exact weighted sensor and branch suppliers are
  external issues #33/#34. Parent Scribe/calibration/gallery/trace chapters
  are consumers, not substitutes for those missing
  estimates.>>|<row|<cell|Public projection>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.continuum_with_position_tests>,
  <verbatim|.existence>, then <verbatim|YangMills.constructed>>|<cell|Core.of_receipts
  retains the same F,L,Q. Public hierarchy takes its Hilbert theory from
  F.action, fields S.Field, labels S.pin, project S.classTokens, phase
  space/measure from F, coefficients from Q, and centeredTrace from
  TraceExtension.center F. No second hierarchy is selected at any public
  bridge.>>>>>

  <section|Public bridge checks actually inspected><label|public-bridge-checks-actually-inspected>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YangMills.regular>: slope is <verbatim|2 *
    Pert.Asymptotics.b0 g.core>, positive by the simple-group Casimir.
    <verbatim|zeroUp_bound> is uniform in p. The fixed local stencil is
    <verbatim|(C.localSection v.1).stencil>, independent of N,p; continuity
    and gauge invariance use the same finite insertion C.O. This is not only
    regularity of its limiting field.

    <item><verbatim|YangMills.wilsonLimit>: fromWilson has full mesh in its
    hypothesis. The projected-token identity holds on separated
    configurations; the compact test vanishes outside that set, so the
    integrands agree there as well.

    <item><verbatim|YangMills.publicOPE>: <verbatim|grouped_eq> uses the same
    finite enumeration of insertions and spectators. The radius threshold
    precedes all allowed positions and viewers; it may depend on fixed
    grade/truncation and labels. No uniformity over all truncation degrees is
    added.

    <item><verbatim|YangMills.publicReconstruction>: label injectivity is at
    each cap; cover follows from the derivative plan and phase injection;
    representative tokens give surjective project. Nonzero action uses the
    nonzero unit and faithfulness. Character continuity uses an actual
    separated-word placement and weak decomposition; mixture uses
    all-character completion. Holomorphy, imaginary roots and product-test
    boundary values are the same chosen heat family. This list identifies the
    caller's exact inputs, not new proofs of them.

    <item><verbatim|YangMills.publicTrace>: the Euclidean two-point function
    is definitionally the chosen centered trace. <verbatim|award_eq>
    identifies the core Lie algebra with the declared real matrix Lie algebra
    and simplifies the common Casimir to <verbatim|3 dim_R(g) / pi^4>.
    Native/public mass-shell profiles coincide term by term, including empty
    products; the existing asymptotic exclusion applies to that finite class.
    No stronger exclusion is inferred.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Completion gate still open><label|completion-gate-still-open>

  A future dependency-closure audit must inspect each retained hypothesis in
  the canonical chapters and map it to an earlier proved result or a checked
  literature reference, on exactly these common data. Merely removing the
  word "input" or updating a cross-reference is insufficient. In particular
  <verbatim|assembly.tex> still states an explicit joint-construction
  assumption and must remain conditional until its entire ledger is
  discharged. After mathematical closure, rewrite that assembly proof and put
  the detailed final audit in the blueprint. Independent source
  correspondence, mathematical review, a logical Section2 outline and
  notation/index work remain separate requirements.

  Commands: scoped <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|sed>, <verbatim|cat> on the files
  above and the existing public-run-binding/evidence and
  assembly/angular-action chapters. One attempted search used nonexistent
  ReconstructionBridge/OPEBridge paths; <verbatim|rg> then located the actual
  declarations in HierarchyBridge. No Lean build or axiom replay was run, no
  Lean file changed, and no whole-tree negative claim was inferred.

  <section|Running coefficient: existing canonical unit to
  integrate><label|running-coefficient-existing-canonical-unit-to-integrate>

  Further bounded inspection12 November: RawAxis.lean full text and
  <verbatim|manuscript/pilots/running-coupling.tex> (YM-000022), plus the
  running subsection of <verbatim|surviving-interval-shooting.tex>. The
  latter proves <verbatim|\|beta_(N,p,i)-hatBeta_i\| \<less\>= epsilon S_i>
  eventually uniformly in N\<gtr\>=i,p from the exact accumulated
  adjacent-step errors. Its hatBeta is the same barBeta+s_G*S_i. Thus its
  output is the input <verbatim|eq:running> of YM-000022 after identifying
  s_G=2b0(G), S_i=log(a_i^-1), and its block sides with that unit's B_i. The
  actual selected-history binding still belongs in the final application.
  This is not a new running-estimate proof task.

  YM-000022 owns the uniform-extraction argument. It is not currently
  included in existence.tex; do not write a duplicate proof. Canonical
  integration and review response remain required. Live issue22
  comment6817309512 (PR32) reports both proposition proofs correct
  conditionally, with requested positivity clarifications (skew-Hermitian
  positive norm; basis independence/nonzero algebra) and additional source
  citations for bare endpoint, denominator/block bound, and alternate
  positivity proof. Its author/reviewer claims were released; no parent edit
  of that unit has been made. A bounded follow-up should address those
  findings under its own scope and renew the fingerprint, then integration
  can include its canonical TeX and bibliography and match the running input.
  <verbatim|YangMills.regular> specializes N=m for the actual bare
  coefficient and is uniform in p. The proxy inverse-square-root coupling
  corollary is not an assertion about a physical renormalized coupling.

  <section|External audit state checked12
  November><label|external-audit-state-checked12-november>

  Issue2 is closed with explicit coordinator acceptance6793308757 of PR7:
  verified prebuilt artifact and kernel replay, not clean source rebuild.
  Issue3 is closed, but its last author handoff still requested independent
  review; closure alone has not been treated here as proof of that review.
  Issue11 external reviewer released claim in6818544207, reporting no
  incorrect interface statement but four requested additions:
  Seed.cutoff/copies/corrected, unselected allWorld contour, every-phase
  Certificate.flux, and full-mesh Ordered distinct from the refinement
  indexing Final. The new phase-ward chapter addresses two of these
  mathematical applications (flux and mixed continuation); the full-mesh and
  Seed/rank clauses retain their separate canonical constructions. The parent
  does not edit issue11's interface file.

  <section|12:25 UTC bounded refresh><label|1225-utc-bounded-refresh>

  <verbatim|free-internal-ward-erasure.tex> now supplies the actual
  threshold-four internal Ward kernel theorem via the grade-four House
  pairing, proper quarter-turn invariance, stress annihilation, same-capacity
  rotational-flux commutator, strict positivity and finite-dimensional ODE.
  Independent bounded math/source pass: be439656, evidence f53ec191. The
  distinct free polar-vector classifier remains pending.
  <verbatim|phase-ward-inheritance.tex> supplies every-character compact flux
  transfer by bounded linear extension; it does not assume that extension is
  positive or multiplicative. Mixed and selected reconstruction applications
  are separate; UniqueHeat is asserted only for the selected phase. See exact
  review records, not these short hashes, before reusing a result.

  <section|13:12 UTC local producer refresh><label|1312-utc-local-producer-refresh>

  The actual shell-node chapter and free external/quiet-charge/collinear
  classifier are now integrated with exact complementary review records.
  Earlier entries listing their local proofs as pending are superseded. Their
  same-history and finite-grade applications are still subject to the closure
  ledger. The selected course audit now identifies Metering.cost as the
  existing Launch supplier; the remaining join is the exact public-run
  specialization of the paid local course, not a new independent Launch
  construction. No global closure is asserted.

  <section|13:38 UTC narrowed selected-course
  result><label|1338-utc-narrowed-selected-course-result>

  Literal-family Binding from Run.bought and generic Paid weakening are now
  proved in selected-course-binding.tex. The attempted stronger recovery of
  the internal franchise receipt for an already fixed R was rejected in
  review. Compare actual exported Chateau rated/warrant/market outputs with
  local consumers; the absence of an exported raw receipt is not a new
  analytic obstruction. The Ward final-binding audit and OPE closure refresh
  provide additional exact interface ledgers, not whole-proof acceptance. See
  their current review records.

